    "summary": "High‑energy second set with monster Truckin' jam and adventurous Other One",
    "blurb": "The Aarhus show is defined by a blistering second set that delivers a towering Truckin' jam and an exploratory Other One sequence. Jerry’s guitar duels with Phil’s bass, while Keith adds late‑night texture. First‑set material suffers from cuts but remains solid enough for completists.",
    "review": "April 16, 1972 finds the Dead at Aarhus University firing on all cylinders, especially once they hit the second set. After a first half riddled with tape glitches and uneven fidelity, the band launches into Good Lovin' and Cumberland Blues before settling into a Deal that segues straight into a truly monumental Truckin'. Jerry and Phil lock in for an unforgettable duet, and the ensuing jam stretches into The Other One, where Keith’s late‑arrival keys sprinkle chimes over spacious drumming from Bill. Me And My Uncle rockets forward with aggressive leads from Bob, and the set closes with back‑to‑back Not Fade Away runs that keep the momentum blazing. Despite the hiss and occasional drop‑outs, the soundboard captures the raw intensity of this European ’72 outing, making it a must‑listen for anyone chasing high‑octane improvisation.",
